{title: Breathe on Me, Breath of God}
{artist: Edwin Hatch / Robert Jackson}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: F}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}
{score: breathe-on-me-breath-of-god.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Breathe on me, [Bb]Breath of [F]God
[Dm]Fill me with [Gm]life a[C]new
[F]That I may [Bb]love what [F]Thou dost love
[Gm]And do what [C]Thou wouldst [F]do
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Breathe on me, [Bb]Breath of [F]God
[Dm]Until my [Gm]heart is [C]pure
[F]Until with [Bb]Thee I [F]will one will
[Gm]To do and [C]to en[F]dure
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Breathe on me, [Bb]Breath of [F]God
[Dm]Till I am [Gm]wholly [C]Thine
[F]Until this [Bb]earthly [F]part of me
[Gm]Glows with Thy [C]fire di[F]vine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Breathe on me, [Bb]Breath of [F]God
[Dm]So shall I [Gm]never [C]die
[F]But live with [Bb]Thee the [F]perfect life
[Gm]Of Thine e[C]ternity [F]
{end_of_verse}
